# Deep tinuë (theme key 'deep', shared/themes.js): long 6x6 puzzles whose stored first move(s) are the only first moves
# a deep proof search found to force a road within the puzzle's length. What is on record for every row: the stored
# first move is proven to force a road in exactly L plies (L = plies), it equals the solver's key, and the search over
# every other first move found none that forces a road as fast. rootUndecided is the certifier's own count of other
# first moves it neither refuted nor found to win within its budget (12 rows have 0).
# rootProof (2026-11-20) closes those: every legal first move other than the key (5,803 over the 49 rows; `moves` on a
# row) was searched as its own position with `deep prove and=1`, with threats only (q=0) and with one quiet attacker
# move allowed (q=1). Each came back "disproved" both ways: noWinAnyDepth of a row's moves have no forced road at any
# depth in that model (searched without a depth limit), noWinWithinL have none within the puzzle's length (p = L-1;
# a slower win is not excluded for these). slowerWins: first moves that do force a road, but more slowly (found at
# q=0 without a depth limit; other slower wins may exist). The run: crux:~/tinue-hard100/runs/deep-proof (summary.txt).
# What is still not on record: lines needing two or more quiet attacker moves after the first move are never searched,
# and a quiet move counts only when it passes the solver's pass test. Other first moves may still win more slowly.
# One {id, plies, key, proof: {tier, L}, rootUndecided, date, rootProof, flaggedRootAlt?} per line. key: the proven first move(s),
# equal to the stored tree's root moves. tier is about the solver's own line, which differs from the stored line on
# most rows: gold = no second winning idea found at its nodes with 7 or more plies left; silver = a second idea wins
# at such a later node. The first-move result is the same for both.
# flaggedRootAlt: root moves that are NOT proven wins but beat the engine defender in 3 of 3 play-outs.
# From the mining pilot of 2026-11-19 (50 candidates; pd654193 is left out: production rejects it as grade D).
# scripts/tag-deep.mjs puts the tag on these ids in the normalized puzzle files; re-run it after regenerating one.
